From c950d8cf353dc47d663fd3b0d7d9b7a3bc971e21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 10:06:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] rc_ipsec: eliminate IPsec command-injection + buffer
 overflows (C2/C3/C7/M1)

Harden the CA/cert handling that embeds nvram-supplied data in generated shell scripts and openssl args:

- cert_import: run cp/openssl via eval() argv (no shell); validate the .p12 filename; feed the import password through -password file: instead of a shell arg; bound the basename copy (fixes the strlen-4 underflow).

- gen_cert: validate remote_id (ddns_hostname_x/WAN IP) as a strict host/IP token and strip shell metachars from the CA CN before writing generate.sh.

- ca_txt_parse: bounded, NUL-safe field copies (no more 32-byte overflow) + snprintf the nvram read; sanitize DN/SAN identity fields.

- ca_gen: write the export password to a 0600 file and reference it via -password file: instead of pass:%s.

Local-only branch; not pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
